      "content": "I see where you're coming from, but it feels like you're suggesting that the \"nationalist\" view is inherently dangerous or prone to becoming fascist. Isn't there a legitimate argument that without some level of national priority, you lose the shared values and common purpose that allow a democracy to function in the first place? It seems like you're treating globalism as the default \"correct\" path and nationalism as a mistake to be avoided.",
